---
title: "Screencasts and narrated video"
---

A `{{< video >}}` gets the browser's own control bar by default: play/pause, a
scrubber, volume, keyboard, native fullscreen, and picture-in-picture, for one
attribute Taliesin adds automatically. The clip stays muted and looping until the
reader presses play. Nothing about it autoplays.

{{< video tour.mp4 caption="The default: native controls, muted and looping until the reader presses play." >}}

## When the clip is narrated

`audio` drops `muted` (you cannot hear a muted narration) and `loop` (a lecture that
silently restarts itself is hostile). `captions=` adds a caption track for the
narration, shown by default.

{{< video tour.mp4 audio captions=tour.vtt caption="With `audio` and `captions=`: a narrated explainer." >}}

## Opting out of the control bar

`controls=false` ships a clip with no control bar at all — and, since nothing
autoplays, no way for the reader to start it either. A deliberate, rare choice for a
purely decorative frame, not a default.

{{< video tour.mp4 controls=false caption="With `controls=false`: no control bar at all." >}}

Flag order is free, so a bare `controls` (redundant now, but still accepted) can come
before the path:

{{< video controls tour.mp4 caption="The flags are not paths, so this still plays `tour.mp4`." >}}
